# Shell scripts must check out with LF endings whatever the developer's core.autocrlf
# says. This repository is developed on Windows, where autocrlf is normally true, and a
# .sh checked out with CRLF fails on macOS and Linux with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M"
# -- an error that names the shell rather than the line endings and reads like a broken
# machine. build/installer/build_mac.sh is run on a Mac by definition, so it would hit
# this on its first use.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Golden receipt fixtures are compared byte-for-byte in SaleReceiptGoldenTest.
# Today they happen to survive autocrlf because git sees a NUL byte inside and
# guesses "binary" on its own; a future fixture with no NUL byte would not be
# so lucky and would get silently rewritten on checkout. Force it instead of
# relying on the guess.
tests/VvCash.Tests/Fixtures/** binary
